          "category": null,
          "questionText": "State the period of $y = \\tan(4x)$.",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "The period of $y = a\\tan(nx)$ is $\\frac{\\pi}{n}$ (for $n > 0$).",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $y = \\tan(4x)$, so $n = 4$. Goal: the period.",
              "Period $= \\frac{\\pi}{4}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "Period $= \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Tangent has period $\\pi$, not $2\\pi$, so divide $\\pi$ by $n$."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex11_q1b",
          "number": "1(b)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "State the period of $y = \\tan\\left(\\frac{2x}{3}\\right)$.",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "The period of $y = a\\tan(nx)$ is $\\frac{\\pi}{n}$.",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $y = \\tan\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x\\right)$, so $n = \\frac{2}{3}$. Goal: the period.",
              "Period $= \\pi \\div \\frac{2}{3} = \\pi \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{3\\pi}{2}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "Period $= \\frac{3\\pi}{2}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Dividing by a fraction less than 1 makes the period longer."
          }
        },
