              "$x = \\frac{u}{3}$: $x = -\\frac{17\\pi}{18}, -\\frac{11\\pi}{18}, -\\frac{5\\pi}{18}, \\frac{\\pi}{18}, \\frac{7\\pi}{18}, \\frac{13\\pi}{18}$.",
              "Check count: period $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ fits 6 times into an interval of length $2\\pi$, giving 6 solutions."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$x = -\\frac{17\\pi}{18}, -\\frac{11\\pi}{18}, -\\frac{5\\pi}{18}, \\frac{\\pi}{18}, \\frac{7\\pi}{18}, \\frac{13\\pi}{18}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Simplify $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ to $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ to recognise the exact value $\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{6}$."
          }
        },
